  "analysis": {
    "frameCostIsCommandBoundNotAreaBound": "Frame p50 is effectively flat across a 5.5x change in device pixels per cell (2.25 -> 12.40), so cost tracks the fixed number of per-cell draw commands rather than the physical area filled.",
    "perFrameStages": "clear, content composite and overlay are each below the 0.05 ms clock granularity at 48x48; the Canvas fill pass dominates the frame.",
    "maxOutliers": "Occasional 6-16 ms maxima are single-frame spikes, not the steady cost: p95 stays at or below 0.5 ms. They are consistent with GC or compositor contention in a headless CPU-rasterised browser and should not be read as the frame budget.",
    "dprNote": "The forced device pixel ratio was not honoured in every row (see dprHonoured). Rows where it was not reflect the ambient ratio of 1, so the high-DPI columns describe a 1x rasterised surface of that CSS size rather than a true 2x or 3x one."
  }
